    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d257">

                <pb facs="0709" n="679" sameAs="frus:frus1949v01/pg679"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">560.AL/5–1949: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chairman of the United
                        States Delegation</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Willoughby</hi>), <hi
                        rendition="#italic">at Annecy</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-05-19T19:00:00-04:00">May 19, 1949—7 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>120. From Brown. Dept agrees your appraisal difficulty situation re MFN Jap
                    Annecy (US Del tel 97<anchor n="1" xml:id="d257-f1"/>). However Dept strongly
                    desires you do everything possible to postpone discussions issue till near end
                    conference in order retain chance for possible favorable developments in
                    meantime. For your info Dept plans present <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >aide-mémoire</hi> Brit Amb and upon being informed presentation you
                    authorized show copy Shackle.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d257-f2"/> Gay coming over
                    via London to discuss further course action.</p>
                <p>Precise course action to be taken end conference can be decided then. Dept
                    studying possibility raising issue context broader objective Jap adherence GATT
                    third round negotiations<anchor n="3" xml:id="d257-f3"/> with modified protocol
                    covering period prior adherence.</p>
                <pb facs="0710" n="680" xml:id="pg680"/>
                <p>Foregoing course based on most serious reconsideration problem following USDel
                    tel 97 and sympathetic view US Del’s position, particularly with respect effect
                    US prestige adverse vote. Can you hold line? While Del authorized discretion
                    decide action in case emergency, consult Dept if possible. Only in event
                    impossible postpone vote and major defeat inevitable is Dept willing that you
                    withdraw item from consideration this session in which case statement should be
                    made along lines para 7 urtel Reply soonest. [Brown.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d257-f1" n="1" xml:id="d257-f1-content">
                <p>Dated May 10, <ref target="#pg670">p. 670</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d257-f2" n="2" xml:id="d257-f2-content">
                <p>R. J. Shackle was Chairman of the British Delegation to the Annecy
                    Conference.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d257-f3" n="3" xml:id="d257-f3-content">
                <p>The series of tariff negotiations that would follow those at Annecy, the latter
                    being the “second round” of multilateral tariff negotiations under the General
                    Agreement (not to be confused with the <hi rendition="#italic">third
                        session</hi> of the Contracting Parties to the General Agreement, also
                    meeting at Annecy). In any event, the third round occurred at Torquay, England,
                    September 1950–April 1951.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
